course: dictionary
lesson: 17
title: Above: higher, more, or earlier
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Above is a small word with several meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one. The most common meaning is higher than something: «The white cloud above a kettle is tiny droplets» means the cloud is higher up than the kettle.
explain: Above can also mean more than a number or a level, as in «above zero» or «above average». When you see a number after above, ask yourself: is this bigger than that number?
explain: In a book, above means earlier on the page. «As shown above» points back to something you have already read. Above all means most importantly, so «above all, stay safe» tells you that safety comes first.
fact: Above means higher than something, such as «blue above and yellow below» on a flag.
fact: Above can mean more than a number: «above zero» means warmer than zero degrees.
fact: Above sea level means a height measured upwards from the sea.
fact: «Above all» means most importantly.
fact: In a building, «the floor above» means the next floor up.
exercise: «Contour lines join points of equal height above sea level.» What does above mean here? | Earlier on the page | *Higher than the sea | More than ten | Most important
exercise: A book says, «as shown above». What does above mean here? | Higher up on a wall | More than a number | *Earlier on the page | Most important of all
exercise: Sam's bedroom is «the floor above» the kitchen. Where is Sam's bedroom? | *On a higher floor | Next to the kitchen | In the garden | Under the stairs
test: «Temperatures above zero are warmer than freezing.» What does above zero mean? | Most important | Earlier in the book | *More than zero, warmer than freezing | Lower than zero
test: In «Above all, tell the truth», what is the most important thing? | *Telling the truth | Reading earlier pages | Being tall | Keeping quiet
exam: Which colour is higher on the Ukrainian flag, as in «blue above and yellow below»? | Red | Yellow | Green | *Blue
